course: dictionary
lesson: 7726
title: Puffball
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A puffball is a round fungus, a bit like a mushroom, but it has no cap and no stalk. It is white or brown, and when it is old it bursts and puffs out a cloud of spores like dust. «Fungi spread by spores, tiny specks like dust» tells you what spores are.
explain: Read the words around puffball for clues. «A giant puffball can hold trillions of them» shows that puffballs are full of spores. «A raindrop or a foot makes them puff out like smoke» shows the cloud coming out. Puff tells you it is a burst of spores, not a ball that is blown up.
explain: The word can also mean anything round, soft and fluffy, like a dandelion clock or a fluffy chick. This is informal, so you will hear it in chatty speech and in stories. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does «a fluffy puffball of yellow chick» still make sense? It does.
explain: Only experts should pick fungi to eat, so never eat a puffball you find outside. Some fungi are dangerous, and you cannot tell by looking.
fact: A puffball is a round fungus with no cap or stalk.
fact: «Giant puffball» means a very large puffball, and it can grow as big as a football.
fact: «Puff of spores» means a small cloud of tiny spores, like dust.
fact: Informally, puffball can mean anything round, soft and fluffy, like a dandelion clock.
fact: Safety: only experts should pick fungi to eat.
exercise: «A giant puffball can hold trillions of spores.» What is a puffball? | *A round fungus with no cap or stalk | A kind of cake made with flour | A long, thin stick | Something in the sky, like a cloud
exercise: «The fluffy chick was a little puffball of yellow.» What does puffball mean here? | *Something round, soft and fluffy | A cloud of dust | A football kicked high | A type of mushroom that you can eat
exercise: «When a puffball is old, it bursts and puffs out a cloud of spores.» What comes out when it is old? | Seeds from a flower | Water from the rain | Feathers and leaves | *Spores, like a cloud of dust
test: «Puff of spores» means what? | *A small cloud of tiny spores | A bag of flour | A sweet smell in the air | A loud noise from the ground
test: Why should you never pick a puffball to eat? | Because puffballs are too heavy to carry | Because they taste of paper | *Only experts should pick fungi to eat, because some are dangerous | Because puffballs only grow at night
exam: How big can a giant puffball grow? | A cat | *As big as a football | A pea | As tall as a house
